This plugin vendors three skills from Matt Pocock's "Skills for Real Engineers":

    https://github.com/mattpocock/skills

    skills/engineering/grill-with-docs   -> skills/grill-with-docs
    skills/productivity/grilling         -> skills/grilling
    skills/engineering/domain-modeling   -> skills/domain-modeling

Upstream commit:

    5b15a47f2d7150f545fbcacbfe381787fc0230dc

Only these three are vendored: `grill-with-docs` is a thin wrapper that runs
`/grilling` using the `/domain-modeling` skill, so the three form the minimal
closure. Upstream ships 36 skills; the rest are deliberately not carried here.

LOCAL MODIFICATIONS
-------------------

These files are NOT verbatim. Five patches apply on top of upstream, in order:

    patches/0001-lowercase-doc-filenames.patch
    patches/0002-askuserquestion-rounds.patch
    patches/0003-drop-context-map.patch
    patches/0004-enable-model-invocation.patch
    patches/0005-capability-conditional-delivery.patch

0001 lowercases the doc-artifact names this repo standardises on - CONTEXT.md ->
context.md, CONTEXT-MAP.md -> context-map.md - and renames the skill's own
reference docs to match (ADR-FORMAT.md -> adr-format.md, CONTEXT-FORMAT.md ->
context-format.md). On a case-sensitive filesystem the uppercase names would be
separate, competing files, so this is a correctness fix rather than a cosmetic one.
It touches `domain-modeling` only.

0002 changes how `grilling` delivers a round, not how it thinks. Upstream asks the
whole frontier as a numbered prose block with emoji headers, which leaves the user
writing an essay to answer it. This routes every round through the AskUserQuestion
tool instead: up to 4 questions per call, 2-4 selectable options each, the
recommendation first. Upstream's design-tree and frontier model is kept intact. It
touches `grilling/SKILL.md` only.

0003 removes the `context-map.md` mechanism from `domain-modeling`: the multi-context
directory tree in SKILL.md, and the map file plus the structure-inference list in
context-format.md. We do not use a map file; the `## Contexts` section of a repo's
AGENTS.md is the map. Note what it deliberately does NOT do. It does not assert that a
repo is single-context, because flow's prep.md forbids inferring that from a missing
map file, and it keeps "when multiple contexts exist, infer which one the topic relates
to", which still applies when the map lives elsewhere. It also rewords SKILL.md's
"Most repos have a single context" lead-in - the surviving half of a deleted contrast -
to stay neutral about context count. 0001 still lowercases
CONTEXT-MAP.md; that hunk builds the intermediate state 0003 then deletes, so the order
matters.

0004 drops `disable-model-invocation: true` from `grill-with-docs`'s frontmatter, so
the model can invoke the skill itself instead of waiting for the user to type the
slash command. It touches `grill-with-docs/SKILL.md` only, and within it only the
frontmatter; the body it leaves verbatim, and 0005 is what later edits that body.
SKILL.md keeps its uppercase name - the skill loader discovers skills by that exact
filename.

0005 makes the two host-specific mechanisms conditional, so the skills still work
where those mechanisms do not exist. Codex has no AskUserQuestion tool and no Skill
tool, and a human can invoke either skill directly on either host. `grilling` now
says to use AskUserQuestion when it is in the tool list and, without it, to ask one
question per turn with numbered options and end the turn - the round-per-turn rhythm
survives, and neither host gets the numbered essay 0002 exists to prevent.
Upstream's one-line `grill-with-docs` body gains a second sentence: without a Skill
tool, read `../grilling/SKILL.md` and `../domain-modeling/SKILL.md` and follow both.
Those paths are relative to the file that names them, which is why they climb a
level. The third hunk flips `allow_implicit_invocation` in
`grill-with-docs/agents/openai.yaml` from false to true. Upstream ships that flag
paired with the `disable-model-invocation: true` that 0004 removes, so this is the
same decision on the Codex side; without it the model can invoke the skill on Claude
and not on Codex.

RE-SYNCING
----------

    1. Copy the three upstream directories over skills/
    2. git apply patches/0001-lowercase-doc-filenames.patch
    3. git apply patches/0002-askuserquestion-rounds.patch
    4. git apply patches/0003-drop-context-map.patch
    5. git apply patches/0004-enable-model-invocation.patch
    6. git apply patches/0005-capability-conditional-delivery.patch
    7. Update the commit SHA above; regenerate any patch that stops applying

To regenerate: commit the upstream-verbatim state, redo the change on top of it,
and `git diff -M` the two commits. Verify by applying every patch to a fresh copy
of upstream and diffing the result against skills/. They must be identical.

